course: dictionary
lesson: 14615
title: The populace
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word populace means all the ordinary people who live in a country or area. It is a formal word, so you will meet it most in history books, the news and exam papers, not in playground talk.
explain: «The king ignored the needs of the populace.» The clue is the king. The populace is everyone who is not the ruler, so it means the ordinary people. In everyday talk, people say «the public» or «the people» instead.
explain: Check by swapping: «The king ignored the needs of the people.» It still makes sense, so people is a good simple swap. Populace is a noun, and we use it with the, as in the populace, not a populace.
fact: Populace is a noun. It means all the ordinary people who live in a country or area.
fact: Populace is a formal word, so it is common in history, news and exam writing.
fact: Everyday words that mean the same thing are «the public» and «the people».
fact: «Populace» means the general public: everyone, not just the rulers or leaders.
fact: A good check is to swap in «people» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The mayor promised to help the populace after the flood.» What does populace mean here? | Animals that live near the river | Only the mayor and the town leaders | *All the ordinary people of the town | A kind of flood water
exercise: Which everyday words could replace populace? | a tall tower | a single policeman | the weather | *the public
exercise: Find the word in «The news spread quickly, and soon the whole populace knew about the new park.» that means all the ordinary people. | news | park | *populace | quickly
test: «The new hospital was built to serve the populace of the whole region.» What does populace mean? | The hospital building itself | Children who are ill | *All the ordinary people who live in the region | Only the doctors and nurses who work there
test: Ella reads: «The government spoke to the populace about the new taxes.» Which swap keeps the meaning? | the government's lawyers | a single speaker | the weather forecast | *the public
exam: «The populace cheered when the old bridge reopened.» Which best explains populace? | The bridge itself, which was old | *The ordinary people of the area, the general public | A kind of cheer that dogs make | Only the people who built the bridge
